        <h2 id="thisMonthTitle">September 1996</h2>
        <p>One new console, one strange three-prong controller, and a living-room ritual about to change. The future still arrived on a Saturday morning, plugged into the family TV.</p>
        <a class="button primary" href="/timeline/1996/#month-sep">Open September 1996</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="monthly-exhibit-object">
        <img src="/assets/media/games/n64-controller-gray.jpg" alt="Gray Nintendo 64 controller with three-prong grip and central analog stick." width="1280" height="1021" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption><strong>Object 09.29.96 · Nintendo 64 controller</strong><span>The North American console launch on September 29 brought a new analog stick into the couch-player vocabulary.</span><a href="/timeline/1996/#month-sep">Read the September case →</a></figcaption>
